### Security Governance

**Defense-in-Depth Security Across Module Boundaries:**

Micro-frontend architectures expand the attack surface by introducing multiple independently deployed JavaScript bundles, CDN distribution, and cross-module communication channels. Comprehensive security governance is essential.

**Module-Level Security Requirements:**

1. **Content Security Policy (CSP)**: Shell application enforces CSP headers preventing XSS attacks across all modules
2. **Subresource Integrity (SRI)**: All module bundles loaded with SRI hashes to prevent CDN compromise
3. **OAuth2/OIDC Authentication**: Consistent authentication across modules with token refresh handled by shell
4. **Supply Chain Security**: npm audit, SBOM generation, and vulnerability scanning for all module dependencies
5. **Container Security**: Kubernetes Pod Security Standards for all module deployments
6. **Secrets Management**: External Secrets Operator with IRSA—no hardcoded credentials in any module

**Cross-Module Security Concerns:**

**1. Event Bus Security:**

Event bus is a potential attack vector for malicious modules injecting crafted events to manipulate other modules.

```typescript
// shell-application/src/events/SecureEventBus.ts
class SecureEventBus {
  private allowedEvents: Map<string, EventSchema> = new Map([
    ['member.selected', { type: 'object', properties: { memberId: { type: 'string' } } }],
    ['claim.submitted', { type: 'object', properties: { claimId: { type: 'string' } } }]
  ]);

  publish(eventName: string, payload: unknown) {
    // Validate event schema
    const schema = this.allowedEvents.get(eventName);
    if (!schema) {
      throw new Error(`Event ${eventName} not registered in allowed events`);
    }

    // Validate payload against schema (prevents injection)
    if (!this.validateSchema(payload, schema)) {
      throw new Error(`Event payload validation failed for ${eventName}`);
    }

    // Sanitize payload (strip scripts, prevent XSS)
    const sanitized = this.sanitizePayload(payload);

    this.eventEmitter.emit(eventName, sanitized);
  }

  private sanitizePayload(payload: unknown): unknown {
    // Strip <script>, javascript:, data: URIs
    return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(payload, (key, value) => {
      if (typeof value === 'string') {
        return value
          .replace(/<script[^>]*>.*?<\/script>/gi, '')
          .replace(/javascript:/gi, '')
          .replace(/data:text\/html/gi, '');
      }
      return value;
    }));
  }
}
```

**2. Module Authentication:**

Ensure only approved modules can load into shell application.

```typescript
// shell-application/src/security/ModuleValidator.ts
class ModuleValidator {
  private async validateModuleSignature(moduleUrl: string): Promise<boolean> {
    // Fetch module manifest with SRI hash
    const manifest = await fetch(`${moduleUrl}/manifest.json`);
    const { integrity, publicKey } = await manifest.json();

    // Verify module signed by approved team
    const signature = await this.verifySignature(integrity, publicKey);
    if (!signature.valid) {
      throw new Error(`Module ${moduleUrl} signature validation failed`);
    }

    return true;
  }

  async loadModule(moduleId: string) {
    const moduleUrl = this.registry.get(moduleId);

    // Validate before loading
    await this.validateModuleSignature(moduleUrl);

    // Load with SRI
    const script = document.createElement('script');
    script.src = `${moduleUrl}/remoteEntry.js`;
    script.integrity = await this.getSRIHash(moduleUrl);
    script.crossOrigin = 'anonymous';
    document.head.appendChild(script);
  }
}
```

**3. CSP Configuration for Multi-Module Architecture:**

```nginx
# nginx.conf - CSP for micro-frontend shell
location / {
    add_header Content-Security-Policy "
        default-src 'self';
        script-src 'self'
            https://claims-mfe.cdn.gainwell.com
            https://eligibility-mfe.cdn.gainwell.com
            https://provider-mfe.cdn.gainwell.com
            'sha256-<shell-inline-script-hash>';
        connect-src 'self'
            https://api.gainwell.com
            https://auth.gainwell.com;
        style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
        img-src 'self' data: https:;
        font-src 'self' data:;
        frame-ancestors 'none';
        base-uri 'self';
        form-action 'self';
    " always;

    add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff" always;
    add_header X-Frame-Options "DENY" always;
    add_header X-XSS-Protection "1; mode=block" always;
    add_header Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" always;
}
```

**4. Kubernetes Network Policies (Module Isolation):**

```yaml
# claims-mfe-network-policy.yaml
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: claims-mfe-network-policy
  namespace: production
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: claims-mfe
  policyTypes:
    - Ingress
    - Egress
  ingress:
    - from:
      - namespaceSelector:
          matchLabels:
            name: istio-system  # Only service mesh can reach pods
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 8080
  egress:
    - to:
      - namespaceSelector:
          matchLabels:
            name: backend-services  # Can only call approved backend APIs
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 443
    - to:  # DNS
      - namespaceSelector:
          matchLabels:
            name: kube-system
      ports:
        - protocol: UDP
          port: 53
```

**5. Secrets Management (No Secrets in Module Bundles):**

```yaml
# claims-mfe-deployment.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: claims-mfe
spec:
  template:
    spec:
      serviceAccountName: claims-mfe-sa  # IRSA for AWS secrets
      containers:
      - name: claims-mfe
        image: claims-mfe:v1.2.3
        env:
          # Secrets injected at runtime—never in bundle
          - name: API_KEY
            valueFrom:
              secretKeyRef:
                name: claims-mfe-secrets  # External Secrets Operator
                key: api-key
        volumeMounts:
          - name: secrets
            mountPath: /etc/secrets
            readOnly: true
      volumes:
        - name: secrets
          csi:
            driver: secrets-store.csi.k8s.io
            readOnly: true
            volumeAttributes:
              secretProviderClass: claims-mfe-secrets
```

**Security Review Process:**

1. **Static Analysis**: SonarQube scans for vulnerabilities in module code
2. **Dependency Scanning**: npm audit + Trivy scan all dependencies
3. **SBOM Generation**: Anchore generates Software Bill of Materials
4. **Penetration Testing**: Annual penetration testing of shell + all modules
5. **Security Architecture Review**: Required for new modules before production deployment
6. **Incident Response**: Security incidents trigger immediate review of all modules (not just affected module)

